    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. we've been looking at the subgrade too. if we're seeing cracks appearing despite having met the compaction specs, could the issue be related to how the bitumen viscosity is reacting to the extreme heat cycles during the curing process? or is that less likely to cause longitudinal cracks specifically?",
      "source": "evaluator"
